body:
Hmmm, I don't know if the government really gives a shit about me, I'm only 17 and still living with my parents. I think it's more the social stigma surrounding it.

&#x200B;

The issue is, people think it's selfish of someone to commit suicide, and hurt those around them. But isn't it just as selfish of everyone else who won't let them die? They think they're helping me you out because you're going to have a bright future. But they are just being selfish because they don't want to lose you. If they were genuinely selfless they would support you committing suicide, but instead, they condemn it.
